  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, Volume is constant,<br /><math><mi>P</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>;</mo></math> as P increases T increases.<br />For process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, the process is adiabatic process,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>&#947;</mi></msup><mo>=</mo></math> Constant<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo></math> Constant.<br />For process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, pressure is constant,<br /><math><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></math>.",
